{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946587-2e-my-houserules-for-crossover","id":946587,"title":"[2E] - my houserules for Crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T17:53:42-07:00","id":946587,"title":"[2E] - my houserules for Crossover","content":"Greetings all,<br /> <br /> I've recently started running a Mage 2E game, and as I love drawing material from all across the World of Darkness lines, and want to use this game to explore some of the deeper and stranger concepts in other games, I'm drafting rules for how mages will be able to interact with some of the more enigmatic forces in other game lines (at least until the Crossover Chronicles is released, I guess).<br /> <br /> Here is the link to my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1p6oy_XrM21QnpkDr-GeJWcqRo8_VfbPZdzJwvhLyY40/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">working draft</a>.<br /> <br /> I'd appreciate feedback, suggestions, and discussion from the community, as I'm sure many of you are far more familiar some of these topics than I am.<br /> <br /> One topic which I would also like to tackle (but haven't written up for the document yet), is Duat and the Twilight frequency of Neter-Khertet. I imagine this as being the Twilight frequency of souls, and as such part of the Death spectrum, and overlaid with ghostly Twilight in some ways: ghosts and twilight objects are visible and touchable from anyone in Neter-Khertet, but the Temak, Amkhata, Apnu, Arisen during their Death Cycles, and the distant mountains with their portal to Duat and the Living world are all exclusive to the Neter-Khertet frequency.<br /> I may leave it as a frequency just falling under Death (with the slight off-shift requiring special knowledge to see), but part of me wants to include another Arcana - either Spirit (due to the somewhat animist horror element to Temak and Amkhata) or Prime (as it's the true intended realm of souls, touched in some ways be the divine).<br /> Does anyone have suggestions on how to handle this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> ~Seraph","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}